  "response": {
    "duration": 60.0,
    "language": "english",
    "text": "Good morning everyone! This is the weekly engineering sync for Project Nimbus. Today is Thursday, and we have four items on the agenda. The Kubernetes migration, the PostgreSQL latency issue, the Q3 OKRs, and the hiring update. Priya, do you want to start with the migration? Sure, thanks Marcus! So the Kubernetes migration is about 70% done. We moved the authentication service, and the billing service to the new EKS cluster last week. The main blocker right now is the Redis cache. When we deployed it with Helm, the persistent volume claims were failing, because of a misconfigured storage class. I opened a ticket, Jira number NIM-482, and I expect it to be fixed by Tuesday. Okay, good. Do we need anything from the DevOps team?",
